Template: cxt/github
Type: string
Description: GitHub username for root SSH public keys:
 Enter a GitHub username, not a URL. Only publicly registered SSH keys from
 https://github.com/USERNAME.keys will be downloaded over verified HTTPS.
 A nonempty set of valid keys is mandatory. No password login is provided.

Template: cxt/keys-confirm
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Trust these SSH public keys for root login?
 GitHub account: ${USERNAME}
 .
 ${FINGERPRINTS}
 .
 These are SSH public keys, not X.509 certificates. Confirm the fingerprints
 against a trusted source. Rejecting returns to GitHub username selection.

Template: cxt/error
Type: error
Description: Preflight cannot continue safely
 ${ERROR}
 .
 No disk has been authorized for partitioning. Correct the problem and retry.
 Network failures are not treated as successful key retrieval.

Template: cxt/disk
Type: select
Choices: ${DISKS}
Description: Entire disk to ERASE for Debian 13:
 All partitions and data on the selected disk will be destroyed. Mounted
 disks, read-only devices and active swap backing disks are excluded.
 .
 ${DETAILS}

Template: cxt/erase
Type: string
Description: Type ERASE to destroy all data on ${DISK}:
 Target: ${DISK}
 ${DETAILS}
 .
 Debian 13 will replace the entire disk, including the old DD installer.
 Type exactly ERASE to authorize this operation. Any other answer returns
 to disk selection. This is the last interactive disk warning.

Template: cxt/late-error
Type: error
Description: Final installation checks did not pass
 ${ERROR}
 .
 The chosen disk has already been repartitioned and Debian installation is
 not complete. Use the installer shell to diagnose the problem, then retry.
 Do not assume the original disk contents remain intact.
